			<div class="content" id="post-content-4070808">
									

<p>I picture Lawler as an aging male researcher who wasn't very good at his job. His &quot;I only read the important documents&quot; retorts are a defense mechanism to make himself sound smarter when he really isn't. In the meantime, he's regularly compared to his much smarter coworkers which can make for a lonely life.</p>
<p>Thus it's kind of fitting that he finds an SCP that's also scared of people but for different reasons.<br />
There's a bond there. Maybe that's why the Foundation chose him instead of a D-class?</p>

